SUMMARY:Fotarida custom and Dormition night\, Kini
LOCATION:Kini\, Syros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 14 August the fishing village of Kini revives the Fotarida\, the old night-fishing lanterns lit along the beach\, followed by an island evening with live music\, and on the 15th the Catholic parish celebrates the Dormition\, as do Galissas\, Pagos\, Piskopio and Chalandriani. Kini's beach tavernas are packed that night\; book.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/syros/#kini-fotarida-custom-and-dormition-night-kini
